WOW-BG3 benilla patch 0098: the see-through leaves ground one can walk on.

Playtest feedback: "some ground turns see through despite me just walking on the surface and looking from an angle
with the camera near the cliff side." 0097 let the capsule cut terrain, and any slope above her feet in the
capsule went. Terrain under 50 degrees now stays, and a cliff still opens. The plugin's cursor keeps the same line.

diff --git a/crates/benilla-assets/src/shaders/terrain.wgsl b/crates/benilla-assets/src/shaders/terrain.wgsl
--- a/crates/benilla-assets/src/shaders/terrain.wgsl
+++ b/crates/benilla-assets/src/shaders/terrain.wgsl
@@ -320,7 +320,10 @@
     // default: a close camera puts the ground right in front of her inside the circle, and ground
     // one can see through is worse than a hill one cannot see past (playtest feedback). A hill
     // between BG3's camera and her is the eye clearance's job, not the circle's.
-    if (wow_light.cut_params.w > 0.5 && wow_cut(in.world_position.xyz, in.uv)) {
+    // Patch 0098: ground one can walk on stays, however the camera looks at it; a cliff goes (50 degrees,
+    // the arena's slope limit). From under the terrain nothing is drawn anyway, so a camera in a hill still sees.
+    let cut_slope = abs(normalize(cross(dpdx(in.world_position.xyz), dpdy(in.world_position.xyz))).y);
+    if (wow_light.cut_params.w > 0.5 && cut_slope <= 0.64 && wow_cut(in.world_position.xyz, in.uv)) {
         discard;
     }
 
